pip is fully restored. Here's what was wrong and what I did:

**Problem:** The `pip` package files were missing from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` — only the `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory remained. The `pip3` binary existed but couldn't import the `pip` module, so every `pip install` failed with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'`.

**Fix:** Extracted the bundled pip wheel (`/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl`) directly into `site-packages/`. This restored the full pip package including all `_internal` and `_vendor` subpackages.

Both `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` now work correctly.

